Cloud platforms continuously evolve through service updates, architectural improvements, and operational enhancements.

Lifecycle management activities include:

* Platform updates
* Feature evaluation
* Security improvements
* Capacity planning
* Documentation updates
* Governance refinement
* Retirement planning

For example, administrators periodically evaluate newly released Azure capabilities that may improve existing production environments.

A real-life use case is enterprises adopting new Azure features to improve security and reduce operational costs.

Lifecycle management keeps cloud environments modern and efficient.
